{"name":"Electrifying Kiss","hex":"#d41c4e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"electrifying","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of electrify"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That electrifies.","Thrilling or startling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electrifying"},{"term":"kiss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch with the lips or press the lips against, usually to show love or affection or passion, or as part of a greeting.","To (cause to) touch lightly or slightly; to come into contact."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A touch with the lips, usually to express love or affection, or as a greeting.","An 'X' mark placed at the end of a letter or other type of message, signifying the bestowal of a kiss from the sender to the receiver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Electrification","blocks":[{"text":"Electrification is the process of powering by electricity and, in many contexts, the introduction of such power by changing over from an earlier power source. In the context of history of technology and economic development, electrification refers to the build-out of the electricity generation and electric power distribution systems. In the context of sustainable energy, electrification refers to the build-out of super grids and smart grids with distributed energy resources to accommodate the energy transition to renewable energy and the switch of end-uses to electricity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/China_electrification_surpasses_OECD.svg/330px-China_electrification_surpasses_OECD.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrification"},{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg/330px-Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Electrification_Staircase%2C_Version_1.0%2C_2040.png/500px-Electrification_Staircase%2C_Version_1.0%2C_2040.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Electrification_Staircase%2C_Version_1.0%2C_2040.png/1280px-Electrification_Staircase%2C_Version_1.0%2C_2040.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Electrification_Staircase%2C_Version_1.0%2C_2040.png/500px-Electrification_Staircase%2C_Version_1.0%2C_2040.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One suggested sequencing of electrification to 2040","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElectrification_Staircase%2C_Version_1.0%2C_2040.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Batteuse_1881.jpg/500px-Batteuse_1881.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Batteuse_1881.jpg/1280px-Batteuse_1881.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp